SUMMARY:Data Days Lightning Talks: Short Talks. Big Ideas. Zero Fluff.
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nWhat happens when you give really s
 mart people 5 minutes and say “go”?\n\nWe’re bringing together MVPs\
 , community builders\, and experts for a rapid-fire series of 5-minute tal
 ks on things they’re excited about right now. No long intros. No overthi
 nking. Just idea after idea after idea. Zero time to get bored.\n\nYou’l
 l hear fresh takes\, clever tips\, and things you didn’t know you needed
  to learn across Microsoft Fabric\, SQL\, Power BI\, and AI. It’s fast\,
  it’s fun\, and by the end you’ll have more ideas than you know what t
 o do with.\n\nPre-requisites:\nFind ways to connect: https://aka.ms/dd/con
 nect\nSee what else is happening during Data Days: https://aka.ms/datadays
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3153
 34476/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260619T220637Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260619T220637Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315274210@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260730T033012Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T140000
SUMMARY:Microsoft IQ Deep Dive with Python: Fabric IQ
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn the final session of our Microso
 ft IQ Deep Dive with Python series\, we’ll explore Fabric IQ and how it 
 connects AI experiences to structured business data.\n\nWe’ll introduce 
 the key concepts behind Fabric IQ\, including ontologies and data agents\,
  and show how they help describe\, organize\, and reason over operational 
 data stored in OneLake.\n\nWe’ll use the Microsoft Fabric API SDK in Pyt
 hon to connect to Fabric IQ\, so that we can programmatically configure on
 tologies and answer questions about our data.\n\nAll code demos will use P
 ython and will be available in an open-source repository for you to deploy
  yourself.\n\nAfter the stream\, join office hours in the [Microsoft Found
 ry Discord](http://aka.ms/aipython/oh) to ask follow-up questions.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3152
 74210/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260615T182759Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260615T182759Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315286034@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260730T033012Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T120000
SUMMARY:¿Qué es MCP y por qué cambia todo en Microsoft Fabric?
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nLa IA ya no solo responde preguntas
 : ahora ejecuta acciones sobre tus datos.\n\nEn esta sesión introductoria
  entenderás qué es el Model Context Protocol (MCP)\, por qué se ha conv
 ertido en el estándar de la industria y cómo Microsoft lo está integran
 do en Fabric como base de su plataforma agéntica.\n\nVeremos la arquitect
 ura cliente-servidor de MCP\, qué son los servidores Local y Remote de Fa
 bric\, y cómo un agente de IA puede descubrir y operar workspaces\, lakeh
 ouses y pipelines usando lenguaje natural. Sin código todavía — el obj
 etivo es que salgas con el mapa mental completo del ecosistema.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3152
 86034/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260616T170751Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T170751Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
